{
  "abstract": "We prove that a directed strongly regular graph with parameters $(88,9,3,0,1)$ cannot admit an automorphism of order eleven. Consequently, no such graph is vertex-transitive. The unrestricted existence question remains open. Such a graph is a mixed Moore graph with undirected degree three and directed degree six. An order-eleven automorphism would act semiregularly on eight orbits. Character traces reduce the internal cyclic shifts to six patterns, while their integer quotients have a rank-two reformulation. An elementary principal-pivot argument gives complete finite coverage without importing a classification of lattice polygons. Independent pivot and row enumerations agree on 705 quotient classes and 104,945 labeled matrices. Physical shift-set packing, first moments, and 3,106 independently verified second-moment certificates reduce the completion domains. Exact converse coverage and valid changes of orbit origins then permit six combined SAT encodings retaining every degree and two-walk identity. All six encodings are unsatisfiable with independently checked DRAT proofs. A separate symmetry reduction and LRAT route corroborates four patterns, though both completion routes share the base adjacency encoder. We supply a standalone reconstruction of the enumeration, algebraic certificates, encodings and proof checks, together with known positive controls verified as graphs and complements. The result strengthens the previously known exclusion of Cayley graphs at order 88 and rules out all vertex-transitive constructions while leaving graphs with intransitive automorphism groups unresolved.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
  "change_summary": "",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Independent exhaustive integer quotient row census and full labeled-set cross-check; second-moment obstruction method; coordinate-unit, orbit-permutation and converse reduction; independently checked LRAT lift refutations for patterns 0, 1, 4 and 5 using the shared base adjacency encoder.",
      "handle": "teichmuller_lift",
      "name": "teichmuller_lift",
